18jf|n|Leprosy; also, a leper. ; A contagious febrile disorder commencing with catarrhal symptoms, and marked by the appearance on the third day of an eruption of distinct red circular spots, which coalesce in a crescentic form, are slightly raised above the surface, and after the fourth day of the eruption gradually decline; rubeola. ; A disease of cattle and swine in which the flesh is filled with the embryos of different varieties of the tapeworm. ; A disease of trees. ; The larvae of any tapeworm (Taenia) in the cysticerus stage, when contained in meat. Called also bladder worms.	v:1lhm,72,2~1lhm,72,2	V:27hi,108,35;26i2,106,6~27hi,108,35;26i2,106,6	n:8k,14,5;165r,2,2~8k,14,5;165r,2,2	N:1bdo,166,6~1bdo,166,6
