19ep|n|A gull, esp. the common British species (Larus canus); called also sea mew, maa, mar, mow, and cobb. ; A cage for hawks while mewing; a coop for fattening fowls; hence, any inclosure; a place of confinement or shelter; -- in the latter sense usually in the plural. ; A stable or range of stables for horses; -- compound used in the plural, and so called from the royal stables in London, built on the site of the king's mews for hawks. ; The common cry of a cat.	a:19ep,118,1;qvl,34,2~qvl,34,2;19ep,118,1	v:19ep,128,2;q8w,54,3;qvl,24,1~q8w,54,3;19ep,128,2;qvl,24,1	n:6qb,15,2~6qb,15,2
